-- title:
--   A supersingular place above every supersingular j-invariant
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $q$ which is prime and a positive natural number $N$ with $q \nmid N$, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$. Inside the field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ consider the element $\mathtt{jqModC}\,K = t^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNum}_K$, the reduction to $K$ of the $q$-expansion of the $j$-function, together with its $N$-fold rescaling $\mathtt{jqNModC}\,K\,N = \mathtt{qExpand}\,K\,N(\mathtt{jqModC}\,K)$, and let $F = \mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ over $K$ generated by these two elements; `jGeomGen K N` denotes the first generator viewed as an element of $F$. Let $a \in K$ lie in `ssJSet q K`, i.e. every Weierstrass curve over $K$ which is elliptic and has $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero affine point $P$ with $q \cdot P = 0$. The assertion is that the following subtype is non-empty: the set of places $w$ of $F$ over $K$ — that is, valuation subrings of $F$ containing $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,F$, different from $F$ itself and principal ideal rings — which lie in `ssPlaces q N K`, meaning $w$ is rational, the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace K N` holds of $w$, and the value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen K N` (the residue of the element, transported back to $K$ along a chosen inverse of $K \to$ the residue field, when the element is in the valuation subring, and $0$ otherwise) belongs to `ssJSet q K`, and which in addition satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen } K\, N) = a$. Given this last equation and the hypothesis on $a$, the third clause in the definition of `ssPlaces` is automatic.
--
--   This is the non-emptiness of the fibre of the supersingular locus of the level-$N$ modular curve in characteristic $q$ above a prescribed supersingular $j$-invariant: over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q \nmid N$, each supersingular $j$ is the $j$-coordinate of at least one rational place of the level-$N$ modular function field at which the moduli generators are regular. It is used in the construction of the Deligne–Rapoport style models at supersingular points, in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isAlgEquivZero_fibre_ofInvertible_of_pullback_zeroSection_iso_unit_of_charP`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isAlgEquivZero_fibre_ofInvertible_of_pullback_zeroSection_iso_unit_of_charP) and in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_widths_componentMap_gluedSpecialization_placeWidthChar_of_isModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_widths_componentMap_gluedSpecialization_placeWidthChar_of_isModel).
